  "database": "rschema_0440",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0440 database is designed to manage and track the status, maintenance, and inventory of devices within an organization. The Device table stores information about each device, including its creation and update times, department, model, group, IP address, person in charge, product name, type, and usage location. The User table contains details about the individuals involved in the device management process, such as their name, role, and contact information. The Device_Status table tracks the current status of each device, including the last update time and any remarks, and is linked to the Device table through a foreign key referencing the device's unique identifier. The Device_Maintenance table records maintenance activities performed on devices, including the content of the maintenance, the person responsible, the result, and the user's satisfaction, and is linked to both the Device and User tables through foreign keys. The Device_Repair_Request table tracks requests for device repairs, including the handling personnel, status, and time, as well as the requester's ID, and is linked to both the Device and User tables through foreign keys. The Device_Inventory table tracks the inventory of devices, including their location and the person responsible for the inventory, and is linked to both the Device and User tables through foreign keys. Each of these tables has a unique identifier or set of identifiers that serve as primary keys, ensuring data integrity and preventing duplicate entries, and some tables also have composite primary keys to account for multiple relationships between entities.",
  "gold_question": "Device Management System Requirements: This is a device management system. In terms of device management, the system supports the input of device information via a mobile application, including product name, device model, person in charge, group, type, usage location, department, IP address, and device images. A unique QR code is generated for each device, enabling a one-device-one-code system, and records the creation and update times of each device. The system also supports the printing and pasting of QR code labels. In terms of user management, the system maintains each user’s basic information, including a unique user ID, name, role, contact information, and account status. For device inventory management, the system supports exporting in-use device information, including device ID, inventory person ID, inventory time, and device location. In terms of device maintenance, staff can submit maintenance requests, including device ID, requester ID, maintenance time, maintenance content, handling status, handling personnel, handling time, and remarks. After submitting a maintenance request, the system assigns maintenance personnel to handle it and records the maintenance details, including device ID, maintenance personnel ID, maintenance time, maintenance content, maintenance results, user satisfaction, and remarks. The system also regularly updates and records the status information for each device, including current status, last update time, and remarks, to ensure the accuracy and efficiency of device management.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0440.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0440\nCREATE TABLE `device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `model` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `group` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `usage_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_status` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `last_update_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `remarks` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_status_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_maintenance` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `responsible_person` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `result` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `satisfaction` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_repair_request` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `handling_personnel` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `request_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_repair_request_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_repair_request_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_inventory` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `responsible_person` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_inventory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_inventory_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
